<title>USA: 99 Cents Only Q2 sales rise to $53.8 mln.</title>
<headline>99 Cents Only Q2 sales rise to $53.8 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CITY OF COMMERCE, Calif. 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>99 Cents Only Stores said Tuesday that second quarter sales reached $53.8 million, up from $43.2 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>For the first half, sales rose to $104.5 million from $85.4 million in the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>In a press release, President David Gold said 99 Cents expects to open at least nine stores this year and that expansion is proceeding according to plan.</p>
</text>
